Now I see the issue! The error shows `item_name='Iron Ore'` on the edge b2, which means propagation is working. But the convergence check is failing because we have 1 splitter, so `logistics_count = 1`, and we're hitting `iteration > 2`.

The problem is that we're setting `changed = True` every time we update an edge's item_name, but the edge `b2` already has `item_name='Iron Ore'` (set in _build_scene from the source miner via the splitter output port). So we're not actually making progress - we're re-setting the same value.

The issue is in Step 1 - we check `if edge.item_name is not None: continue` but then we also `continue` after setting the item_name from source. But the splitter ports keep getting updated which triggers `changed = True` even when their item_name is already correct.

Let me fix the splitter port update to only set `changed = True` when actually changing:

